From 55a5335d3672d0bc0968d22d6a7b972ea9c97488 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: girayk <girayk@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:10:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(council): fork MoA into LLM Council virtual provider
 (karpathy/llm-council semantics)

- agent/council_loop.py: 3-stage loop (parallel member answers -> anonymized
  peer review / optional dedicated judge with strict FINAL RANKING parsing ->
  chairman acts with tools+streaming); turn-scoped fan-out cache, stage
  deadlines, alternation-rejection retry; reuses moa_loop helpers by import
- provider=='council' dispatch wired at every moa site in agent/ (42 gates)
- hermes_cli: council_config/council_cmd/subcommands.council (hermes council
  list|configure|delete), virtual picker row, CANONICAL_PROVIDERS entry,
  GET/PUT /api/model/council, config defaults, banner, validation, backup
  protection, runtime_provider council://local shortcut
- tui_gateway: council.member/review/phase/synthesizing progress events +
  contract payloads; gateway contract artifacts regenerated
- desktop: Settings > Model > Council page (members add/remove, judge slot,
  chairman slot, preset management), 'Council presets' model-menu section,
  live stage rendering, i18n en
- MoA untouched and byte-identical; no regressions vs baseline (14 pre-existing
  env-caused failures identical before/after)
